      "content": "Equally unsafe to assume a mild headache indicates no serious issue, especially because internal bleeding often does not present with immediate external signs. Waiting until the morning with a recent head injury while on Eliquis removes your chance to intervene before a bleed worsens, and many hospitals will bill you for the same evaluation regardless of whether you come during business hours or evenings. A medical professional might tell you to be conservative initially, but that decision should be made by them after an exam, not by your own judgment as a measure to avoid delay. Please consider the risk of a delayed, potentially life-threatening bleed outweighs temporary concerns over wait times.",
